<title>USA: New York Fed director of press relations resigns.</title>
<headline>New York Fed director of press relations resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The staff director of press relations at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, Bart Sotnick, has resigned to take a new job in the private sector.</p>
<p>&quot;I've decided to resign,&quot; Sotnick said.</p>
<p>Sotnick, who spent 12 years working at the New York Fed, refused to reveal the name of his new employer. He said, however, his new job &quot;is in the private industry and it's going to be an editorial-type position.&quot;</p>
<p>Sotnick said his replacement has not been chosen yet. He leaves the Fed on December 11.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
